WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.415 --> 00:00:17.436
boys looked for a way to get to the Pharaoh’s pyramid.

2
00:00:17.456 --> 00:00:20.858
“There!” Akhom pointed.

3
00:00:23.379 --> 00:00:25.801
“We can sail to the Pharaoh’s pyramid in that boat!”

4
00:00:25.821 --> 00:00:34.349
“It looks like half a banana,” laughed Vinnie, describing the large sailing ship.

5
00:00:35.989 --> 00:00:38.890
“No. That small one,” corrected Akhom.

6
00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:42.691
The big boat was pulling a smaller one.

7
00:00:44.512 --> 00:00:47.272
Men were loading baskets onto the smaller boat.

8
00:00:48.453 --> 00:00:51.954
“Someone special must be going to visit the site,” said Akhom.

9
00:00:51.974 --> 00:00:53.854
“How do you know?”

10
00:00:54.615 --> 00:00:55.255
asked Vinnie.

11
00:00:55.275 --> 00:01:00.580
“All those baskets are food,” explained Akhom.

12
00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:03.342
“They only prepare that much food for the royal family.

13
00:01:04.423 --> 00:01:06.604
They must be going for a visit to the pyramid.”

14
00:01:07.105 --> 00:01:09.186
“Let’s jump on!”

15
00:01:09.806 --> 00:01:10.447
said Vinnie.

16
00:01:11.588 --> 00:01:15.871
The boys snuck into the small boat and hid among the food baskets.

17
00:01:17.151 --> 00:01:20.834
In the larger boat, twenty men picked up their long oars.

18
00:01:22.135 --> 00:01:23.876
They pushed and pulled the oars.

19
00:01:25.437 --> 00:01:29.340
The wind filled the gigantic sail and the small boat followed.

20
00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:33.501
The boys sailed down the Nile.

21
00:01:34.762 --> 00:01:39.224
From the boat, Vinnie could see all kinds of interesting things off shore.

22
00:01:42.786 --> 00:01:45.888
A farmer pushed a wooden plough through a field of wheat.

23
00:01:47.369 --> 00:01:49.710
Another large ship sailed beside them.

24
00:01:51.051 --> 00:01:53.412
It carried a huge white block of stone.

25
00:01:53.432 --> 00:01:55.173
“What’s that?”

26
00:01:55.713 --> 00:01:57.034
he whispered to Akhom.

27
00:01:57.054 --> 00:02:01.877
“That’s one of the blocks used for building a pyramid,” Akhom answered.

28
00:02:01.897 --> 00:02:05.659
“Pyramids are made of hundreds of heavy blocks of stone.”

29
00:02:05.679 --> 00:02:10.021
“That must take a lot of time and work,” said Vinnie.

30
00:02:10.942 --> 00:02:15.524
“Some say we make more stones than there are stars,” explained Akhom.

31
00:02:15.544 --> 00:02:18.886
“Thousands of people work on the Pharaoh’s pyramid.

32
00:02:19.406 --> 00:02:21.687
They started to build it before I was born.”

33
00:02:21.707 --> 00:02:25.069
“When will it be finished?”

34
00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:28.031
Vinnie asked in a surprised voice.

35
00:02:29.231 --> 00:02:30.012
Akhom shrugged.

36
00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:32.320
“Perhaps in a couple of years.

37
00:02:33.381 --> 00:02:34.801
Maybe by the time I marry.”

38
00:02:37.502 --> 00:02:41.523
Suddenly Vinnie saw a pair of blinking eyes staring from the water.

39
00:02:41.543 --> 00:02:44.984
“Akhom! Is that a crocodile?”

40
00:02:45.624 --> 00:02:46.384
Vinnie pointed.

41
00:02:47.645 --> 00:02:48.765
Akhom shook his head.

42
00:02:48.785 --> 00:02:50.805
“No, that’s a hippo.

43
00:02:51.346 --> 00:02:52.866
Look! There’s a crocodile!”

44
00:02:54.086 --> 00:02:56.887
Akhom pointed to a reptile lying in the sand.

45
00:02:59.268 --> 00:03:02.522
Further on the shore, they could see the Pharaoh’s pyramid.

46
00:03:03.623 --> 00:03:04.884
The boats slowed down.

47
00:03:06.245 --> 00:03:08.146
Men shouted orders at each other.

48
00:03:08.166 --> 00:03:12.990
“When we reach the shore, run for the pyramid,” Akhom instructed.

49
00:03:15.152 --> 00:03:20.556
When the boys jumped off the boat, Vinnie was surprised by the sight of the pyramid in real

50
00:03:20.636 --> 00:03:23.339
life. “Whoa!”

51
00:03:23.899 --> 00:03:27.442
he said, as he stopped to look up at the huge structure.

52
00:03:28.543 --> 00:03:32.350
Facing the sunset, the pyramid looked very majestic.

53
00:03:33.831 --> 00:03:37.293
Each side of its base was the length of two soccer fields.

54
00:03:38.434 --> 00:03:42.697
Though it seemed already quite tall, the workers were adding more blocks.

55
00:03:43.818 --> 00:03:47.760
Vinnie saw thousands of men pulling the heavy white blocks of stone.

56
00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:52.143
The boys climbed a ramp that led into the pyramid.

57
00:03:53.084 --> 00:03:57.027
Behind them, a voice shouted, “You, boys, stop!

58
00:03:57.447 --> 00:03:58.428
What are you doing here?”

59
00:03:59.308 --> 00:03:59.949
"The guards!”

60
00:04:00.230 --> 00:04:01.111
yelled Akhom.

61
00:04:01.131 --> 00:04:02.153
“Run, Vinnie!

62
00:04:02.233 --> 00:04:07.802
Run!” The boys ran up a ramp toward the pyramid.

63
00:04:08.864 --> 00:04:10.927
The guards followed closely behind.
